          "text": "Another Claude session sent a message:\n<teammate-message teammate_id=\"diag-259\" color=\"purple\" summary=\"#259 root-caused: dupe/missing resume race + fix proposal\">\nRoot-caused. Two distinct, code-verified bugs share one symptom (strict-mode `getByText(ANSWER)` violations). Read-only — nothing modified.\n\n## Bug A (CONFIRMED, high confidence): concurrent resume connections merge into one message with duplicate text parts\n\n**Trigger chain:**\n1. `apps/web/app/(chat)/components/chat-page.tsx:297-313` — `PersistedChatSession` always passes `resume: true` into `useChat(...)`.\n2. `@ai-sdk/react` (`node_modules/.../@ai-sdk/react/src/use-chat.ts:149-153`):\n   ```js\n   useEffect(() => {\n     if (resume) { chatRef.current.resumeStream(); }\n   }, [resume, chatRef]);\n   ```\n   **No cleanup function, and the call isn't awaited.** Under React 19 StrictMode (on by default, unconfigured in `apps/web/next.config.ts`), every dev-mode mount runs an effect body **twice** (no teardown needed since there's no cleanup) — so `resumeStream()` fires **twice** per mount, back-to-back, fire-and-forget.\n3. Both calls hit `GET /chats/:id/stream` independently. Server side, `apps/api/src/chats/chats.controller.ts:124-128` → `RunStreamBridgeService.createUiMessageStreamResponse` (`apps/api/src/runs/run-stream-bridge.ts:308-334`) builds a **brand-new translator with `cursor = 0`** per HTTP connection — no single-flight/dedup guard. Both connections independently replay the whole run from scratch, both stamping `start.messageId = runId` (same surrogate id, `run-stream-bridge.ts:110`/`330`).\n4. Client side, `ai@6.0.217`'s `chat.ts:649/658`: `const lastMessage = this.lastMessage;` is read **after** each call's own `await reconnectToStream(...)` resolves — so the two resume calls race. Whichever call's snapshot lands *after* the other has already pushed its own placeholder assistant message (role `'assistant'`) will, in `createStreamingUIMessageState` (`ai/src/ui/process-ui-message-stream.ts:52-76`), **reuse that message object** (`lastMessage?.role === 'assistant' ? lastMessage : {new}`) — via `this.state.snapshot()` = `structuredClone` (`@ai-sdk/react/src/chat.react.ts:72`), so it's a deep clone, not a live reference.\n5. The second connection's own `activeTextParts` map (per-connection state) starts **empty**, so it has no knowledge of the part already cloned in. `case 'text-start'` (`process-ui-message-stream.ts:369-380`) **unconditionally `state.message.parts.push(textPart)`** — no dedup, no check for an existing open/closed text part. Result: `message.parts` = [connection A's frozen partial text (whatever it had at clone time), connection B's own freshly-replayed, eventually-complete text] — **exactly the observed ARIA snapshot** (one `generic` container, two sibling `paragraph`s: prefix + full sentence).\n6. `write()`'s merge logic (`chat.ts:698-709`) matches by `activeResponse.state.message.id === this.lastMessage?.id` (both are `runId` once each connection processes its own `start` chunk) → `replaceMessage`, so this collapses into **one** message slot, not two bubbles — matches the bug report (\"one bubble, two paragraphs\") precisely.\n\n**Also explains the \"missing\" variant on retry**, via a related TOCTOU gap: `apps/api/src/runs/run-execution.service.ts` `onFinish` handler calls `finishRun()` (marks the run terminal + commits, line ~873) **before** `recordAssistantTurn()`/`persistAssistantMessage()` commits (line ~892) — two separate commits. If a resume/reload lands in that window: `GET /messages` (history) doesn't have the assistant row yet, and `resumeChatStream` → `RunsRepository.findActiveByChatId` (`apps/api/src/runs/runs-repository.ts:98-119`, filters `notInArray(status, [completed,failed,cancelled,expired])`) already sees the run as terminal → 204 → `chat.ts:633-635` \"no active stream found, so we do not resume\" → nothing renders, ever (no retry/backoff anywhere in this path).\n\n**Verified directly a