leParallelism: false` is already set — ordering is serial; the problem is shared thread state, not concurrency.\n\n## Candidate fixes\n\n1. Find and fix the leaking teardown: identify which file leaves a `runs` consumer polling (worker-harness-based suites, `queue.integration`, and any AppModule boot under the `all` worker profile are the candidates) and make its teardown deterministic — stop pg-boss before ending the pool.\n2. Failing that, restore a process boundary for the queue-touching subset (a second vitest invocation), which is what the old three-invocation script effectively provided.\n\n## Why it matters\n\nThe `rls` job is the repo's security gate (FORCE RLS proven against a worst-case owner role). A gate that goes red for reasons unrelated to the change under test is the exact failure mode that let the browser-e2e job rot for 11 days.\nEOF\ngh issue create --title \"Integration suite is cross-file flaky: leaked pg-boss worker from an earlier test file\" --body-file /tmp/claude-1000/-home-leon0399-Projects-llame/535318ad-af01-431c-8824-5411e9f64c95/scratchpad/issue5.md --label bug 2>&1 | tail -1",
