r-completion (a `chat.titled` notification or a client follow-up invalidation) remains a separate follow-up, as does formalising the new invariant as an `openspec/specs/durable-runs` delta if you want it normative beyond SPEC.md §9.3.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `pnpm --filter api test` — 507 passed\n- `pnpm --filter api test:integration` — 257 passed (re-run in full after the lock-order rework)\n- typecheck, lint, format clean\n- browser e2e is CI's call: the refresh specs are confounded on this machine (devtools locale bug), and they are the specs this is expected to stabilise\nEOF\ngh pr edit 265 --body-file \"$SCRATCH/pr-body2.md\" 2>&1 | tail -2",
